🎯 Brick Breaker Game

A classic Brick Breaker game developed in C++ using SFML. Control the paddle, bounce balls, break bricks, and try to survive as long as possible. Features multiple balls, levels, score system, lives, and sound effects.



🎮 Game Rules

Paddle Control: Left Arrow → Move left, Right Arrow → Move right

Serve Ball: Press SPACE to start or serve a new ball

Balls: Max 3 balls, duplicate randomly on brick collision

Bricks: Destroy to earn 10 points per brick

Levels: Clear all bricks to advance

Lives: Start with 3; lose a life if all balls fall

Game Over: Occurs when no lives left; press SPACE to restart

Sounds: Paddle hit → line.wav, Brick hit → land.wav

⚙️ Requirements

C++17 or higher

SFML 2.5 or higher

Font file: ARIALI.TTF

Sound files: line.wav, land.wav

💻 How to Compile & Run
g++ main.cpp -o BrickBreaker -lsfml-graphics -lsfml-window -lsfml-system -lsfml-audio
./BrickBreaker


Make sure all resources (ARIALI.TTF, line.wav, land.wav) are in the same folder as main.cpp.

📂 File Structure
BrickBreaker/
├── main.cpp       # Game source code
├── ARIALI.TTF     # Font file
├── line.wav       # Paddle hit sound
├── land.wav       # Brick hit sound
├── screenshot.png # Optional screenshot for README
└── README.md      # This file

📈 Features

Smooth paddle movement and ball physics

Multiple balls with random duplication (max 3)

Brick destruction and scoring system

Level progression with increasing difficulty

Lives and game over handling

Sound effects for paddle & brick interactions

🔧 How to Play

Launch the game.

Press SPACE to serve the ball.

Move the paddle to keep the balls in play.

Destroy all bricks to progress to the next level.

Avoid losing all balls to prevent Game Over.

Press SPACE to restart after Game Over.

🌟 Notes

Only 3 balls can be active at a time.

Balls duplicate randomly when hitting bricks.

Make sure the font and sound files are in the same directory as the executable.